ng to use your  voice you were going to use your voice  in a stronger way than you've ever been  able to because most of you are 18 or  you're going to turn 18 so you're going  to vote and she wrapped her message up  with a call to action you are going to  have empathy for those who don't see the  world through the same lens that you do  because with this diverse and vibrant  and open mind and as I know the  teachings and immaculate heart are I  know you know that black lives matter so  I am already excited for what you are  going to do in the world you are  equipped you are ready we need you and  you are prepared  Markel and her husband Prince Harry  stepped down from their roles as senior  Royals on March 31st and relocated to LA  with their one-year-old son Archie where  they'd been quarantine ndu to the corona  virus pandemic but before Markel  delivered her message to the all-girls  Catholic school she was already  inspiring some of the students there who  started the group students for Floyd  what are you hoping to achieve through  this organization what are your goals  well my goals right now are obviously  just going to protest and showing that  we can get a large group of kids  together to take action and make  initiative and then we're also leading a  bunch of cleanups to kind of help with  the aftermath of the protest cleaning up  graffiti helping out shops all that  stuff ET spoke with a 17 year old  founder of the initiative who said  Markel has had a huge impact on her  i've been so inspired by her and also  just my school community as well because  everything that she speaks about and  stands for i think was really instilled  in her at our school  [Music]
 

